0 — relocate the coordination loop (done 2026-09-13).** The\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:676:**Phase 0′ — parity over the transactor's medium.** *Gated on the\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:677:`run-on-stream` partial-session fix landing first* (Phase 0's pending item):\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:769:## 8. Open questions\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:795:## Appendix A. Review findings and their resolution\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:801:| F1 | Phase 0′'s `pr-str`/`read-string` round trip of a live session cannot pass: `BTSet` prints elements-only, a storage handle is unprintable (glm P2) | Phase 0′ round-trips the *checkpoint value* instead and compares `restored-indexes` to the live trees |\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:802:| F2 | Draining the recording handle is unsafe on the resumed-checkpoint path on the JVM: `-store-tree!` rewrites the wrapper's restore source and a soft-ref'd root refaults through the drained handle (glm P2) | §4.1 states the invariant (refaults resolve against durable content, never the handle) and pins index-session roots `:strong`; re-restore after flush rejected because materialization is asynchronous; Phase 0′ test |\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:812:| N2 | \"Survives a forced GC\" is not a deterministic test; soft clearing cannot be forced (glm P3) | Phase 0′ pins the hazard both ways through the `:test` ref-type and `clear-test-refs!` |\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:818:| N3 | The \"wrong construction\" assertion is vacuous off the JVM, where the read path already defaults `:strong` (glm P3) | Phase 0′ asserts against `bt/default-ref-type*` and gates that assertion to the JVM |\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:824:| A1 | Resolution omits the `m` slot; a macro log's `m = ev` (a negative event id) would stay unresolved and disconnect provenance; `local-datom?` cannot catch it (astra P1) | §2.2 step 2 resolves all three identity slots including `m`-only tempids; §3.1 matrix has an `m` row; Phase 0′/2 tests |\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:827:| A4 | \"Retain the exact list\" is not per-payload progress; the `run-on-stream` progress defect bites an indexer whose round finishes a publication then throws (astra P2) | §4.1 state machine `{:payloads :next}`, advance per `ok`, terminal outcomes throw with `:next` preserved; at-most-once per staged occurrence stated as the guarantee; Phase 0′ gated on the observer fix |\ndocs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md:832:| A9 | Manifest equality is not a valid acceptance test: `from-sequential` and `conj` partition the same rows differently (JVM probe) (astra P2) | Phase 0′ requires logical equality — rows, counts, query results, valid restore — with enough rows to force splits |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:22:## 0. Decisions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:75:## 1. Axioms and invariants\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:125:## 2. Representation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:127:### 2.1 The macro entity\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:148:### 2.2 The definition form\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:166:### 2.3 The call site\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:179:### 2.4 The root fact and the codec\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:198:## 3. The expander (`yin.vm.macro`)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:200:### 3.1 Contract\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:367:### 3.2 The algorithm\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:462:### 3.3 Executing the macro lambda\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:609:### 3.4 Tail positions in expansion output\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:641:### 3.5 Guards\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:664:## 4. Provenance\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:666:### 4.1 The expansion event\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:704:### 4.2 Identity across media\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:729:### 4.3 Authority\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:741:## 5. The expander as an observer\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:805:**Prerequisite on the observer (Phase 0).** `run-on-stream` today publishes\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:837:## 6. Compositions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:839:### 6.1 `yin.repl`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:862:### 6.2 `yang.clojure`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:871:### 6.3 Non-homoiconic frontends\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:880:### 6.4 Build pipelines\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:889:### 6.5 Cross-platform\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:899:## 7. Phased implementation roadmap\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:901:### Phase 0 — Spec and codec\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:927:### Phase 1 — Expander and yang\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:989:### Phase 2 — REPL composition\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1004:### Phase 3 — Cross-language verification\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1014:### Reserved\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1029:## Appendix A. Deviations from prior documents, with reasons\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1093:## Appendix B. Risks the implementer should watch\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1123:## Appendix C. Round-2 review findings and their resolution\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1136:|    |                                                                                | Phase 0 deliverable on `dao.stream.observer`: return progress with the error         |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1171:| 15 | Root fact unconditional vs \"compile output unchanged\" (glm P3-6)               | Phase 0 test reworded \"modulo the root fact\"                                     |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.macro.md:1208:|    | continue silently (glm P3-2); load vs flush failure must carry different       | depends on where the failure was; Phase 0 tests                                  |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
