{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '741,836p' docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md; sed -n '899,928p' docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md; sed -n '535,597p' docs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md; sed -n '1,100p' test/dao/stream/observer_test.cljc; rg -n 'ex-message|defn ex-info|defn ex-data|run-on-stream' src/cljc/yin src/cljc/dao .clojuredart deps.edn docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '741,836p' docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md; sed -n '899,928p' docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md; sed -n '535,597p' docs/design/dao.space.index.as-observer.md; sed -n '1,100p' test/dao/stream/observer_test.cljc; rg -n 'ex-message|defn ex-info|defn ex-data|run-on-stream' src/cljc/yin src/cljc/dao .clojuredart deps.edn docs/agents/build-n-test.md\"","aggregated_output":"## 5. The expander as an observer\n\nThe expander is driven by `dao.stream.observer/run-on-stream` with\nits state in the `:consumer` slot — the coordination inspects no field of\nthe consumer, so it drives an expander as readily as a VM:\n\n```\nexpander = {:ctx ctx\n            :out writer        :out-staged  nil|datoms\n            :log writer|nil    :log-staged  nil|datoms\n            :forwarded 0       ; batches appended ok to :out since the last drain\n            :errors []}        ; expansion failures since the last drain\n\nready?       (fn [x] (and (nil? (:out-staged x)) (nil? (:log-staged x))))\nload         (fn [x batch]\n               (let [r (expand-batch batch (:ctx x))]\n                 (-> x (assoc :ctx (:ctx r))\n                       (assoc :out-staged (when (= :ok (:status r)) (:datoms r)))\n                       (assoc :log-staged (when (:log x) (:log r)))\n                       (cond-> (= :error (:status r)) (update :errors conj (:error r))))))\nrun          flush                    ; below\ndrain-errors (fn [x] [(assoc x :errors [] :forwarded 0) {:errors (:errors x) :forwarded (:forwarded x)}])\n```\n\n`:errors` and `:forwarded` are **read-and-reset** by the driver through\n`drain-errors`, once per driver round, after `run-on-stream` returns and\nbefore the driver decides what to do next. Nothing else clears them; a\ndriver that never drains sees an ever-growing list, which is its bug, not a\nstuck expander (the cursor has moved on regardless).\n\n**Flush** delivers each staged payload to its own medium and clears *that*\nslot on `ok`, independently:\n\n+----------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| Outcome on a medium                          | Effect on its slot                                                                                                      |\n+==============================================+=========================================================================================================================+\n| `ok`                                         | slot ← nil; for `:out`, `:forwarded` += 1                                                                               |\n+----------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| `full`                                       | slot kept; expander stays not-ready; the same payload is retried next round. `full` may be permanent; retention is      |\n|                                              | correct, progress is the composition's to arrange                                                                       |\n+----------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| `closed`, `invalid-value`, `transport-error` | legitimate protocol outcomes that this forwarder cannot continue from: throw, preserving the original outcome and both  |\n|                                              | slots' state in the thrown value, so the composition decides                                                            |\n+----------------------------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n\nOnce a medium has answered `ok` its payload is never appended again by an\nordinary retry, so `out = ok, log = full` re-tries only the log. A batch\nthat expands with `:error` stages nothing for `program-out` and stages the\nevent for the log; the source cursor advances (the load returned), the\nfailure is on the log, and the driver drains it. Program and log are\nindependent media: this design offers *at-most-once per medium* and batch\norder per medium under ordinary retries, not atomic visibility across the\ntwo and not crash recovery; a composition that needs atomicity commits both\nto one `dao.space` transaction (§4.2).\n\n`run-on-stream`'s contract supplies the rest: a `full` leaves the expander\nnot-ready with the exact payload staged, so the next round retries the\nappend before observing again; `gap` on `program-in` is counted by the\nobserver and is the composition's policy, as for any observer. What remains\na *throw* out of `load` is a forwarder defect (codec failure, index\nfailure); the cursor does not advance and the batch is re-read, which is\nthe correct behaviour for a bug and the wrong one for bad input — hence\ndecision 11.\n\n**Prerequisite on the observer (Phase 0).** `run-on-stream` today publishes\nits successor session only on return. If it forwards A, then B's load or run\nthrows, the caller still holds the pre-A session and a retry forwards A again\n(reproduced by the round-2 review against the current observer). This is a\ndefect of the generic coordination, not of this design — a VM loader that\nthrows on B after loading A has the same problem — and it is fixed there.\nThe fix **keeps the throw** and carries the partial session in the\nexception's data: `(ex-info … {:session {:observer o' :consumer c'} …})`. A\nreturn-shaped `{:observer :consumer :error}` was considered and rejected: every\nexisting caller reasons \"a throw means the round failed\", and a value-shaped\nerror would let an un-updated caller continue silently past a defect. With\nthe throw kept, recovery is opt-in: a caller that catches resumes from\n`:session`; one that does not keeps today's semantics. The carried session\nmust distinguish *where* the failure was: a **load** failure carries the\ncursor before the failing batch (it will be re-read); a **run/flush**\nfailure after a successful load carries the cursor *after* that batch and\nthe `:consumer` as the failing `run` left it (for the expander: its partially\nflushed slots), so a retry neither re-reads B nor re-appends what B already\ndelivered. This document depends on that fix and does not work around it.\n\n```\n  yang ──▶ program-in ──observe──▶ expander ──append──▶ program-out ──observe──▶ evaluator\n                                       │\n                                       └──append──▶ log (events, m-tagged output)\n```\n\nEvery evaluator observes `program-out` through its unchanged loader:\n`ast-walker/vm-load-program`, `linearize/loader ∘ semantic`, the stack\ncompiler. None composes anything macro-related.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Phased implementation roadmap\n\n### Phase 0 — Spec and codec\n\n- This document. `macro-design.md` and `cross-language-macro.md` amended to\n  point here. The divergence register's macro item becomes: \"user-defined\n  macros are expanded by a process between media, never by an evaluator;\n  call sites are ordinary applications; `eval` does not expand.\" Its Macros\n  section records the deviations of Appendix A.\n- `yin.vm`: `schema` gains `:yin/root` and `:yin/macro-name`, drops\n  `:yin/phase-policy`, `:yin/phase`, `:yin/capability`, `:yin/source-call`,\n  `:yin/macro`, `:yin/expansion-root`, `:yin/error` (event attributes move\n  to the expander's emitter). `ast->datoms-with-root` emits the root fact;\n  `index-datoms` honours it (last wins, dangling error); the codec drops the\n  `:yin/macro-expand` arms and the `:phase-policy` handling.\n- `ast-walker`: the `:lambda` arm and `datoms->ast` continue to ignore\n  `:macro?`; nothing else changes. The namespace docstring's \"no macro\n  branch\" remark becomes the statement of decision 1.\n- `dao.stream.observer/run-on-stream`: throw with the partial session in\n  `ex-data` (§5 prerequisite); existing callers are unchanged. Tests: A\n  forwarded, B's load throws — the carried cursor is before B and a retry\n  from it leaves exactly one A on the destination; A forwarded, B's `run`\n  throws — the carried cursor is after B and `:consumer` is as `run` left it; a\n  terminal read after a successful batch carries the post-batch session.\n- New `test/yin/vm_test.cljc` for the codec: root fact wins; dangling\n  root errors; heuristic fallback unchanged; `compile` output unchanged\n  *modulo the root fact* for macro-free programs (the fact is unconditional).\n\n### Phase 1 — Expander and yang\n\ntherefore never a special case: the composition resumes from the last\n*verified* checkpoint and re-folds the suffix. Promotion proves the\nsnapshot is reopenable; that the checkpoint *record* itself is recoverable,\nand that the suffix after `c` is still retained on the medium, are the\ncomposition's separate obligations. A candidate captured from a session\nwhose `:ids` is `:shared` is **never promoted**: it may be published and\ncaptured for inspection, but under this contract it is a snapshot, not a\ncheckpoint, and `restore` would refuse it anyway (below).\n\n**Resumption is bound.** `restore` refuses a checkpoint whose `:mode` or\n`:schema-hash` differ from the session being constructed, **and refuses one\nwhose `:ids` was `:shared`**: a session-local snapshot of a shared allocator\nis stale the moment any sibling allocates after it, and restoring it would\nre-mint ids siblings already hold (session A checkpoints at 20, B allocates\n20–29, A restores and allocates 20 again). Recovery of a shared allocation\ndomain is a composition-level checkpoint over *every* session that shares\nit, and is deferred (§8); this note's checkpoint/restore contract covers\nindependently allocated sessions only. For those, `restore` rebuilds the\nfour trees lazily through a session-constructed `:strong` `kv-storage` over\nthe durable store (§4.1 — not the query read path) and reinstates `:ids`,\n`:batch`, `:max-t`, and `:rejected` on the consumer; the composition\nre-attaches the observer at `c` with `:ingress-gaps` reinstated (a partial\nindex stays partial after restart; a fresh zero would make §3.2's offset\ncheck look safe again). Re-attaching *at a cursor* is a small addition to\n`dao.stream.observer/attach`, which mints at `:oldest` today: a third\narity `(attach attach! descriptor {:cursor c :ingress-gaps g})` returns\n`{:stream handle :cursor c :ingress-gaps g}` — the kept cursor, which\n`dao.stream.md` already says \"covers repositioning\", validated by the\ntransport on the first `next`, and the gap count seeded from the checkpoint\nrather than reset to `0`. Then folding continues;\nnothing is replayed from the origin.\n\n**The watermark.** The transactor's `create!` needs `0` for an empty\nhistory, else one plus the greatest `t` retained. A checkpoint covering\n`t ≤ 10` cannot answer that alone if transactions through `t = 12` exist\nafter its cursor. So the answer is `:max-t` — a writer-time summary derived\nfrom the folded rows at capture, causally bound to `:cursor`, never derived\nfrom observer ordinals — *plus the fold of the retained suffix after `c`*\nbefore writes are enabled; the watermark is then `0` if `:max-t` is still\n`nil` (nothing folded, the transactor's empty case) and `max-t + 1`\notherwise, and an empty checkpoint reopened in-process yields `0`, not `1`.\nThree cases, distinct:\n\n- **Same logical stream, reopened in-process** (the writer-task restart\n  `dao.space.md` §Fault Tolerance names): restore the checkpoint, fold the\n  suffix from `c` to `blocked`, then derive as above. This is the O(suffix)\n  relief the transactor asked for.\n- **Process restart over a durable medium** (`dao.stream.file.md`, cursors\n  survive): the same, over the reopened medium.\n- **Process restart over a memory-log**: a new, empty logical stream with a\n  new identity; the checkpoint's cursor names nothing on it, the session\n  starts at `:oldest`, and the watermark is the transactor's today (`0` for\n  empty history).\n\n\"One truth\" is honoured rather than assumed: `:max-t` is not a second\ncounter that can disagree with the log; it is the log's own `t`, summarized\nat a named cursor and only ever advanced by folding the log. Where the\ncheckpoint *record* lives — on the observed medium or beside the manifest\nin `dao.jing` — remains open (§8); its validity conditions above do not.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Relationship to the transactor and to `publish-index!`\n(ns dao.stream.observer-test\n  \"Generic observer tests: a fake unary attacher and a hand-rolled reader.\n\n   No transport namespace is required here, because the observer's contract\n   ends at `dao.stream`. The ring-buffer realization is exercised by the\n   ast-walker and REPL suites, which compose the observer over\n   `dao.stream.ringbuffer`.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]))\n\n\n(defn- throws-ex-data\n  \"Evaluate thunk; return its ex-data, or nil when it did not throw.\"\n  [thunk]\n  (try (thunk) nil\n       (catch #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object) e\n         (ex-data e))))\n\n\n(defn- reader-medium\n  \"A reader-surface medium over an atom of values.\n\n   `next` answers `ok` for positions at or above the eviction floor, `gap`\n   below the floor with the floor as the recovery cursor, `end` at the tail\n   once closed, and `blocked` at the tail while open. The writer and closable\n   surfaces record their calls so a test can prove the observer never performs\n   them. Returns `{:handle h :evict! f :close-medium! f :used atom}`.\"\n  [& [values]]\n  (let [data (atom {:values (vec (or values [])), :floor 0, :closed? false})\n        used (atom [])]\n    {:handle\n     (reify\n       stream/IDaoStreamReader\n       (cursor\n         [_ anchor]\n         (if (= :dao.stream/oldest anchor)\n           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n            :dao.stream/cursor {:pos (:floor @data)}}\n           {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-anchor}))\n\n       (next\n         [_ cursor]\n         (let [{:keys [values floor closed?]} @data\n               pos (:pos cursor)]\n           (cond\n             (not (map? cursor))\n             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n\n             (< pos floor)\n             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/gap,\n              :dao.stream/cursor {:pos floor}}\n\n             (< pos (count values))\n             {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n              :dao.stream/value (nth values pos),\n              :dao.stream/cursor {:pos (inc pos)}}\n\n             closed? {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/end}\n             :else {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked})))\n\n\n       stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n\n       (append!\n         [_ v]\n         (swap! used conj [:append v])\n         {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n\n\n       stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n\n       (close!\n         [_]\n         (swap! used conj [:close])\n         {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))\n     :evict! (fn [floor] (swap! data assoc :floor floor))\n     :close-medium! (fn [] (swap! data assoc :closed? true))\n     :used used}))\n\n\n(defn- recording-attacher\n  \"A unary attach capability over one handle, recording every call.\"\n  [handle]\n  (let [calls (atom [])]\n    {:attach! (fn [descriptor]\n                (swap! calls conj descriptor)\n                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n                 :dao.stream/handle handle})\n     :calls calls}))\n\n\n(defn- attach-to\n  \"Attach one observer to `medium` through a fresh unary capability.\"\n  [medium]\n  (let [{:keys [attach!]} (recording-attacher (:handle medium))]\n    (observer/attach attach! {:dao.stream/type :test/medium})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:736:(defn- ast-walker-run-on-stream\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:738:  (engine/run-on-stream vm\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:755:  (run [vm] (ffi/maybe-run vm ast-walker-run-on-stream))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:304:(defn run-on-stream\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/server.cljc:38:         {:error (ex-message e)})))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:7:   each batch to `vm-load-program` through `run-on-stream`. `eval` converts\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:717:   hands to `dao.stream.observer/run-on-stream` alongside\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/rpc/retry.cljc:52:                                         (= \"Request timeout\" (ex-message e)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:199:       #?(:clj (or (ex-message error) (str error))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:200:          :cljs (or (ex-message error) (.-message error) (str error))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:201:          :cljd (or (ex-message error) (str error)))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:116:       #?(:cljd (or (ex-message error) (str error))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:117:          :cljs (or (ex-message error) (.-message error) (str error))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:118:          :clj (or (ex-message error) (str error)))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl/core.cljc:437:              (observer/run-on-stream {:observer observer0,\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc:31:   Exports exactly `attach`, `observe-next`, and `run-on-stream`.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc:194:  (throw (ex-info (or (ex-message e) (str e))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc:199:(defn run-on-stream\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The load-failure and terminal-read cursor boundaries look correct. The run-failure path carries the state returned by `load`, but §5 requires any progress made inside the failing flush. I’m checking that distinction against the tests and the host exception APIs."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md deps.edn; rg --files .clojuredart | head -20; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc | sed -n '180,270p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/observer_test.cljc | sed -n '445,520p'; sed -n '260,315p' test/dao/stream/observer_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md deps.edn; rg --files .clojuredart | head -20; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc | sed -n '180,270p'; nl -ba test/dao/stream/observer_test.cljc | sed -n '445,520p'; sed -n '260,315p' test/dao/stream/observer_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # Run all tests (JVM, Node/CLJS, Dart/CLJD)\nbb test:clj          # JVM tests only (or: clj -M:test)\nbb test:cljs         # ClojureScript / Node tests (via shadow-cljs :cljs alias)\nbb test:cljd         # ClojureDart tests (requires flutter on PATH)\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\n## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n\nWrite tests before implementing features (TDD).\n\nTests define the contract and expected behavior. Implementation follows from the tests, not the other way around.\n\nWhen implementing a feature or fix:\n1. **Red phase**: Write the test first — define what should happen.\n2. **Green phase**: Implement the minimum code to pass the test.\n3. **Refactor phase**: Refactor if needed while keeping tests green.\n\nThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n\n## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n\nA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\n\n1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\n   ```sh\n   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\n   ```\n\n2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\n   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\n\n3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\n   Common patterns:\n   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\n   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\n   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\n\n4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"run\" \"yin.repl/-main\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"run\" \"yin.repl/-main\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           :telemetry-server {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.vm.telemetry-server.jvm\"]}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                          :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                          :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n            :main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                          :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                          :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n            :main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}\n           :atzu {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"agent.tzu\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n;; clj -M:test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yang.python-test\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n\n;; clj -X:clean\n\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n\n\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:cljd watch \n;; mise exec -- flutter run \n\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\n;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \n;; emulator -list-avds\n\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \"yin.*\"   # only yin namespaces\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\n.clojuredart/cache/81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488/cljd_helper/pubspec.yaml\n.clojuredart/cache/81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488/cljd_helper/pubspec.lock\n.clojuredart/cache/81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488/cljd_helper/bin/analyzer.dart\n   180\t;; Coordination\n   181\t;; =============================================================================\n   182\t\n   183\t(defn- carry-session\n   184\t  \"Rethrow `e`, keeping the throw and carrying the partial session in the\n   185\t   exception's data.\n   186\t\n   187\t   The original message and data are preserved, the original exception is\n   188\t   the cause, and `:session` is added. Recovery is opt-in: a caller that\n   189\t   does not read `:session` keeps the old semantics — a throw means the\n   190\t   round failed — and a caller that catches resumes from the carried\n   191\t   session, which names the furthest progress the round had made where the\n   192\t   failure happened.\"\n   193\t  [session e]\n   194\t  (throw (ex-info (or (ex-message e) (str e))\n   195\t                  (assoc (ex-data e) :session session)\n   196\t                  e)))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(defn run-on-stream\n   200\t  \"Coordinate one `{:observer observer :consumer consumer}` session over the\n   201\t   attached medium, returning the updated session.\n   202\t\n   203\t   The consumer is any value the three supplied functions agree on. `ready?`\n   204\t   decides when it may accept another batch, `load` hands it one observed\n   205\t   batch and returns the successor consumer, and `run` lets it do whatever\n   206\t   work a loaded batch implies — evaluate, expand, index, forward — and\n   207\t   returns the successor. This is coordination, not interpretation: no field\n   208\t   of the consumer is inspected, so any consumer shape can be driven.\n   209\t\n   210\t   A consumer that is not ready runs first, and observation follows only if\n   211\t   it becomes ready. A ready consumer observes one batch; `gap` commits the\n   212\t   recovery cursor and continues; `blocked` and `end` return the session.\n   213\t   After a batch loads and runs, a consumer that is ready again observes the\n   214\t   next batch, and one that is not returns the session without another read.\n   215\t\n   216\t   A `load` or `run` that throws still propagates — the throw is kept — but\n   217\t   carries the partial session in the exception's data under `:session`, so\n   218\t   recovery is opt-in. Where the failure happened decides the carried\n   219\t   session: a throwing `load` carries the cursor *before* the failing batch,\n   220\t   so a retry re-reads it; a throwing `run` carries the cursor *after* the\n   221\t   loaded batch and the consumer `load` returned — the state the failing\n   222\t   `run` left in the coordination's hands — so a retry neither re-reads the\n   223\t   batch nor repeats work already delivered; a terminal read after processed\n   224\t   batches carries the session those batches produced. A consumer whose\n   225\t   input can be bad should therefore return that as data from `load` rather\n   226\t   than throw, and reserve the throw for its own defects.\"\n   227\t  [session ready? load run]\n   228\t  (loop [{:keys [observer consumer]} session]\n   229\t    (if-not (ready? consumer)\n   230\t      (let [consumer' (try (run consumer)\n   231\t                           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   232\t                             (carry-session {:observer observer, :consumer consumer} e)))]\n   233\t        (if (ready? consumer')\n   234\t          (recur {:observer observer, :consumer consumer'})\n   235\t          {:observer observer, :consumer consumer'}))\n   236\t      ;; The load is the step's effect, so the cursor advances only once it has\n   237\t      ;; returned: a throwing load propagates before any successor exists, and\n   238\t      ;; the session it carries names the cursor before the failing batch.\n   239\t      (let [observed (try (observe/step (:stream observer)\n   240\t                                        (:cursor observer)\n   241\t                                        (fn [batch]\n   242\t                                          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   243\t                                           :dao.stream.observer/loaded\n   244\t                                           (load consumer batch)}))\n   245\t                          (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   246\t                            (carry-session {:observer observer, :consumer consumer} e)))]\n   247\t        (case (:status observed)\n   248\t          :advance (let [loaded (:dao.stream.observer/loaded (:effect observed))\n   249\t                         ;; The batch was observed and loaded before the run, so\n   250\t                         ;; a throwing run carries the post-batch cursor and the\n   251\t                         ;; loaded consumer.\n   252\t                         observer' (assoc observer :cursor (:cursor observed))\n   253\t                         consumer' (try (run loaded)\n   254\t                                        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   255\t                                          (carry-session {:observer observer', :consumer loaded} e)))]\n   256\t                     (if (ready? consumer')\n   257\t                       (recur {:observer observer', :consumer consumer'})\n   258\t                       {:observer observer', :consumer consumer'}))\n   259\t          :gap (recur {:observer (adopt-gap observer observed),\n   260\t                       :consumer consumer})\n   261\t          ;; :retry (blocked) and :ended retain the cursor and end the round.\n   262\t          (:retry :ended) {:observer observer, :consumer consumer}\n   263\t          (try (observation-terminal observed observer)\n   264\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n   265\t                 (carry-session {:observer observer, :consumer consumer} e))))))))\n   445\t        (is (= {:pos 3} (:cursor (:observer session))))))))\n   446\t\n   447\t\n   448\t(deftest a-run-failure-carries-the-session-after-the-loaded-batch-test\n   449\t  (let [loaded (atom [])\n   450\t        refused (atom false)\n   451\t        medium (reader-medium [[:a] [:b] [:c]])\n   452\t        observer (attach-to medium)\n   453\t        load (fn [consumer batch]\n   454\t               (swap! loaded conj batch)\n   455\t               (assoc consumer :pending batch))\n   456\t        run (fn [{:keys [pending] :as consumer}]\n   457\t              (when (and (= [:b] pending) (not @refused))\n   458\t                (reset! refused true)\n   459\t                (throw (ex-info \"run refused batch B\" {:batch pending})))\n   460\t              (-> consumer\n   461\t                  (update :delivered conj pending)\n   462\t                  (assoc :pending nil)))\n   463\t        ready? (fn [consumer] (nil? (:pending consumer)))\n   464\t        data (throws-ex-data #(observer/run-on-stream\n   465\t                                {:observer observer,\n   466\t                                 :consumer {:pending nil, :delivered []}}\n   467\t                                ready?\n   468\t                                load\n   469\t                                run))]\n   470\t    (testing \"The throw keeps its data and carries the partial session\"\n   471\t      (is (= {:batch [:b]} (dissoc data :session)))\n   472\t      (let [carried (:session data)]\n   473\t        (is (= {:pos 2} (:cursor (:observer carried)))\n   474\t            \"The batch was observed and loaded before the run failed, so the\n   475\t                carried cursor is after B\")\n   476\t        (is (= {:pending [:b], :delivered [[:a]]} (:consumer carried))\n   477\t            \"The consumer is the loaded state the failing run left in hand\")))\n   478\t    (testing \"A retry from the carried session resumes, repeating nothing\"\n   479\t      (let [session (observer/run-on-stream (:session data)\n   480\t                                            ready?\n   481\t                                            load\n   482\t                                            run)]\n   483\t        (is (= [[:a] [:b] [:c]] @loaded)\n   484\t            \"Each batch loaded exactly once: B was not re-read\")\n   485\t        (is (= [[:a] [:b] [:c]] (:delivered (:consumer session)))\n   486\t            \"Each batch delivered exactly once: the resumed run delivered B\n   487\t                and A was not re-delivered\")\n   488\t        (is (= {:pos 3} (:cursor (:observer session))))\n   489\t        (is (nil? (:pending (:consumer session))))))))\n   490\t\n   491\t\n   492\t(deftest a-terminal-read-after-a-processed-batch-carries-the-session-test\n   493\t  (let [reads (atom [{:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   494\t                      :dao.stream/value [:a],\n   495\t                      :dao.stream/cursor {:pos 1}}\n   496\t                     {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error}])\n   497\t        handle (reify\n   498\t                 stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   499\t                 (cursor [_ _]\n   500\t                   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok,\n   501\t                    :dao.stream/cursor {:pos 0}})\n   502\t\n   503\t                 (next [_ _] (let [answer (first @reads)]\n   504\t                               (swap! reads rest)\n   505\t                               answer)))\n   506\t        {:keys [attach!]} (recording-attacher handle)\n   507\t        c (scripted-consumer (set (range 10)))\n   508\t        observer (observer/attach attach! {:dao.stream/type :test/medium})\n   509\t        data (throws-ex-data #(observer/run-on-stream\n   510\t                                {:observer observer, :consumer (:vm c)}\n   511\t                                (:ready? c)\n   512\t                                (:load c)\n   513\t                                (:run c)))]\n   514\t    (testing \"The batch was processed before the terminal read\"\n   515\t      (is (= [[:a]] (:batches @(:state c)))))\n   516\t    (testing \"The terminal throw carries the post-batch session\"\n   517\t      (is (= :dao.stream/transport-error (:dao.stream/outcome data)))\n   518\t      (let [carried (:session data)]\n   519\t        (is (= {:pos 1} (:cursor (:observer carried))))\n   520\t        (is (= (:vm c) (:consumer carried)))))))\n            {:keys [attach!]} (recording-attacher handle)\n            observer (observer/attach attach! {:dao.stream/type :test/medium})\n            data (throws-ex-data #(observer/observe-next observer))]\n        (is (some? data))\n        (is (= outcome (:dao.stream/outcome data))\n            \"The original outcome is preserved\")))))\n\n\n(deftest independent-observers-keep-independent-cursors-test\n  (let [medium (reader-medium [[:a] [:b]])\n        o1 (attach-to medium)\n        o2 (attach-to medium)\n        r1 (observer/observe-next o1)\n        r2 (observer/observe-next o2)]\n    (is (= (:batch r1) (:batch r2))\n        \"Both observers read the same history from their own oldest\")\n    (is (= [:b] (:batch (observer/observe-next (:observer r1))))\n        \"The first observer's progress does not move the second's cursor\")\n    (is (= [:b] (:batch (observer/observe-next (:observer r2)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; run-on-stream\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- scripted-consumer\n  \"A consumer with no evaluator fields: a plain map plus recording\n   coordination functions, proving `run-on-stream` inspects no walker state.\n\n   `ready-at` is the set of step numbers at which the consumer may accept\n   another batch; `run` advances the step. `load` records each\n   batch and throws on one carrying ::poison.\"\n  [ready-at]\n  (let [state (atom {:step 0, :events [], :batches []})]\n    {:vm {:shape ::not-an-ast-walker}\n     :state state\n     :ready? (fn [_vm] (contains? ready-at (:step @state)))\n     :load (fn [vm batch]\n                     (swap! state (fn [s]\n                                    (-> s\n                                        (update :events conj :load)\n                                        (update :batches conj batch))))\n                     (when (some #{::poison} batch)\n                       (throw (ex-info \"poison batch\" {:batch batch})))\n                     vm)\n     :run (fn [vm]\n               (swap! state (fn [s]\n                              (-> s\n                                  (update :step inc)\n                                  (update :events conj :run))))\n               vm)}))\n\n\n(defn- coordinate\n  \"Run one session over `medium` with consumer `c`.\"\n  [c medium]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
